{# Offline draft recovery partial
 Place this partial inside your admin layout or content form mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 so users see a recovery option.
 The element must be present with id `offline-draft-recover-placeholder` for the JS integration to use it.
#}
<div id="offline-draft-recover-placeholder" class="hidden p-4 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 text-amber-700 border border-amber-200 flex justify-between items-center ">
 <div>
 <strong>Unsynced draft available</strong>
 <div>Saved <span class="draft-saved-at"></span></div>
 </div>
 <div class="flex gap-2">
 <button type="button" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold transition px-3 py-1.5 text-xs bg-indigo-600 text-white hover:bg-indigo-700 restore-draft-inline-flex">Restore</button>
 <button type="button" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-lg px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold transition px-3 py-1.5 text-xs text-slate-600 hover:bg-slate-100 dismiss-draft-inline-flex">Dismiss</button>
 </div>
</div>



